<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Centennial Park, Sydney</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Centennial Park is a large public park in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a>, opened in 1888 to mark the centenary of the British colony of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a>. On 1 January 1901 the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> was proclaimed there and its first governor-general and ministry were sworn in, an event marked by the Federation Pavilion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/centennial-park-sydney.jpg" alt="Centennial Park, Sydney" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sardaka · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afternoon_light_Centennial_Park_005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
